.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt S2I_ASN1_IA5STRING 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm i2s_ASN1_IA5STRING ,
.Nm s2i_ASN1_IA5STRING ,
.Nm i2s_ASN1_INTEGER ,
.Nm s2i_ASN1_INTEGER ,
.Nm i2s_ASN1_OCTET_STRING ,
.Nm s2i_ASN1_OCTET_STRING ,
.Nm i2s_ASN1_ENUMERATED ,
.Nm i2s_ASN1_ENUMERATED_TABLE ,
.Nm i2s_ASN1_UTF8STRING ,
.Nm s2i_ASN1_UTF8STRING
.Nd convert objects from/to ASN.1/string representation
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509v3.h
.Ft char *
.Fo i2s_ASN1_IA5STRING
.Fa "X509V3_EXT_METHOD *method"
.Fa "ASN1_IA5STRING *ia5"
.Fc
.Ft ASN1_IA5STRING *
.Fo s2i_ASN1_IA5STRING
.Fa "X509V3_EXT_METHOD *method"
.Fa "X509V3_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "const char *str"
.Fc
.Ft char *
.Fo i2s_ASN1_INTEGER
.Fa "X509V3_EXT_METHOD *method"
.Fa "const ASN1_INTEGER *a"
.Fc
.Ft ASN1_INTEGER *
.Fo s2i_ASN1_INTEGER
.Fa "X509V3_EXT_METHOD *method"
.Fa "const char *value"
.Fc
.Ft char *
.Fo i2s_ASN1_OCTET_STRING
.Fa "X509V3_EXT_METHOD *method"
.Fa "const ASN1_OCTET_STRING *oct"
.Fc
.Ft ASN1_OCTET_STRING *
.Fo s2i_ASN1_OCTET_STRING
.Fa "X509V3_EXT_METHOD *method"
.Fa "X509V3_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "const char *str"
.Fc
.Ft char *
.Fo i2s_ASN1_ENUMERATED
.Fa "X509V3_EXT_METHOD *method"
.Fa "const ASN1_ENUMERATED *a"
.Fc
.Ft char *
.Fo i2s_ASN1_ENUMERATED_TABLE
.Fa "X509V3_EXT_METHOD *method"
.Fa "const ASN1_ENUMERATED *e"
.Fc
.Ft char *
.Fo i2s_ASN1_UTF8STRING
.Fa "X509V3_EXT_METHOD *method"
.Fa "ASN1_UTF8STRING *utf8"
.Fc
.Ft ASN1_UTF8STRING *
.Fo s2i_ASN1_UTF8STRING
.Fa "X509V3_EXT_METHOD *method"
.Fa "X509V3_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "const char *str"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions convert OpenSSL objects to and from their ASN.1/string
representation.
This function is used for
.Sy X509v3
extensions.
.Sh NOTES
The letters
.Sy i
and
.Sy s
in
.Sy i2s
and
.Sy s2i
stand for "internal" (that is, an internal C structure) and string
respectively.
So
.Sy i2s_ASN1_IA5STRING Ns
.Xr 3
converts from internal to string.
.Pp
It is the caller's responsibility to free the returned string.
In the
.Sy i2s_ASN1_IA5STRING Ns
.Xr 3
function the string is copied and the ownership of the original string
remains with the caller.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Sy i2s_ASN1_IA5STRING Ns
.Xr 3
returns the pointer to a IA5 string or NULL if an error occurs.
.Pp
.Sy s2i_ASN1_IA5STRING Ns
.Xr 3
return a valid
.Vt ASN1_IA5STRING
structure or NULL if an error occurs.
.Pp
.Sy i2s_ASN1_INTEGER Ns
.Xr 3
return a valid string or NULL if an error occurs.
.Pp
.Sy s2i_ASN1_INTEGER Ns
.Xr 3
returns the pointer to a
.Vt ASN1_INTEGER
structure or NULL if an error occurs.
.Pp
.Sy i2s_ASN1_OCTET_STRING Ns
.Xr 3
returns the pointer to a OCTET_STRING string or NULL if an error occurs.
.Pp
.Sy s2i_ASN1_OCTET_STRING Ns
.Xr 3
return a valid
.Vt ASN1_OCTET_STRING
structure or NULL if an error occurs.
.Pp
.Sy i2s_ASN1_ENUMERATED Ns
.Xr 3
return a valid string or NULL if an error occurs.
.Pp
.Sy s2i_ASN1_ENUMERATED Ns
.Xr 3
returns the pointer to a
.Sy ASN1_ENUMERATED
structure or NULL if an error occurs.
.Pp
.Sy s2i_ASN1_UTF8STRING Ns
.Xr 3
return a valid
.Vt ASN1_UTF8STRING
structure or NULL if an error occurs.
.Pp
.Sy i2s_ASN1_UTF8STRING Ns
.Xr 3
returns the pointer to a UTF-8 string or NULL if an error occurs.
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn i2s_ASN1_UTF8STRING
and
.Fn s2i_ASN1_UTF8STRING
were made public in OpenSSL 3.0.
